{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790966790,"nonce":"0vqrJTffIDRaaAlBbcJMsJwr/AA=","title":"f64-\u003ef32 IntoReactive wraps signals in a Computed, demoting signal bindings to derived","message":"`IntoReactive\u003cf32\u003e` for the f64 sources (landed `1e2a3c52`) narrows by wrapping\nthe source in a `Computed\u003cf32\u003e`. That converts a **signal binding** into a\n**derived binding**.\n\nProperty bindings on a `Reactive::Bound` source register against a `SignalId`\n(`register_typed(state.signal_id(), …)`) and fire on every set. A\n`Reactive::Computed` source registers a derived binding, and derived bindings do\n**not** refresh Div-backed properties. So a bound f64 prop compiles, renders its\nbuild-time value, and never updates.\n\nConfirmed visually: `cn.Skeleton(w/h/rounded = \u003cfsm ctx f64\u003e)` and\n`cn.Separator(opacity = …)` are static. `cn.Progress(value = …)` still works\nbecause `ProgressConfig` routes its Computed arm through `bind_transform_from`,\nwhich does listen to the derived notifier -- Div's `w`/`h`/`rounded`/`opacity`\ndo not.\n\n**Attempted and reverted:** mirroring the f64 signal into an f32 signal via an\n`effect`, returning `Reactive::Bound(mirror)`. Setters stay untouched and the\nsignal path is restored in principle, but the mirror does not track: the\neffect's write to the mirror goes through the re-entrancy queue and is never\ndrained, so it holds its initial value. `effect()`'s own doc mentions draining\nqueued writes after `create_effect`; a working mirror needs that drain on every\nrun, not just the first.\n\n**FIXED 155a922e** with a read adapter on `State\u003cT\u003e` (`State::mapped`). The\nstate keeps the **source** signal's id -- so binding registration and `deps()`\nsubscribe to exactly what they did before -- and only the read is redirected.\nAn f64 signal is handed out as a `State\u003cf32\u003e` narrowing per read, so the f64\nimpls return `Bound` rather than `Computed`. No new `Reactive` variant, so none\nof the 31 `Reactive::Bound(` match sites had to move.\n\nConsidered and rejected: adding a `Reactive` variant (31 sites), and a\n`TypedPendingBinding\u003cf64\u003e` with an f64-typed writer (needs a per-setter f64\npath).\n\nThe `Computed\u003cf64\u003e` arm is separately stuck: it cannot mirror (reading a derived\ninside an effect takes the re-entrant cached path) and derived-to-derived deps\nare untracked, so `computed { } : f64` into a cn widget is initial-value-only\nregardless. See gotcha reactive numeric width generics.\n\nRelated: project cn reactive prop migration, feedback stateful container.","files":null}]}